# NOTICE

**nvcodec-blackwell** is a **port of the H.264 part of [mickys/nvenc](https://github.com/mickys/nvenc)**
(MIT) to NVIDIA Blackwell (GB20x, RTX 50). mickys/nvenc drives the NVIDIA NVENC/NVDEC engines from user
space and exposes them through VideoToolbox on macOS for the 40-series (Ada) cards; its codec cores and
VideoToolbox plug-in ABI are the basis of this repository. This port adds GB20x support for that H.264 path
and a faster read-out. All credit for the original NVENC/NVDEC work belongs to mickys.

The GB20x code path covers device-id `0x2a00`–`0x2fff`, but it has been **tested on real hardware only
with an RTX 5070 Ti (GB203)**. No other RTX 50 card is verified; see README for details.

**Scope: only H.264 is ported, enabled and verified.** `src/` retains the full upstream source tree
(`hevcdec.c`, `av1dec.c`, `vp9dec.c`, `mpeg2dec.c`, `vc1dec.c`, …) because the encoder links the shared
`enc.c` / `dec.c` / `rm.c` code. Those files are the untouched mickys/nvenc baseline: they are neither
ported to Blackwell nor registered by the VideoToolbox plug-ins, and carry the same MIT licence.

- `src/`, `tools/`, `src/vt/` derive from mickys/nvenc, MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 mickys.
- `src/blocklinear.c` (Blackwell 64-byte × 16-row tile layout, banded multithreaded untiling), `src/dec.c`
  layout selection, `src/vt/vtnencvt.c` GB20x detection and the VideoToolbox property reporting are
  additions made in this port, under the same MIT licence.
- `src/vtdec.c` is the H.264 decoder plug-in here; `src/vt/nvencvt_dec.c` in the upstream tree is a
  multi-codec plug-in and is not used here.

